judge_raw_output:
Adding a diversity objective is the highest-value, low-risk next change: the run shows very low absolute performance (performance mean = 0.0166, std = 0.0005, best = 0.0186) and a marked contraction of diversity (distance_from_center mean = 0.2132, std = 0.0008; distance mean dropped by -0.0662). The registered scorer parameter_spread exists but is unused. I will add parameter_spread as a maximize objective with a meaningful weight to encourage per-candidate variability and counter premature convergence.

<decision>{
  "failure_location": "objective",
  "root_cause_hypothesis": "The objective set does not sufficiently reward parameter-space diversity: distance_from_center alone (weight=0.25) has not prevented collapse toward the center and the parameter_spread scorer is not currently used, so exploration incentives are weak relative to the optimizer's implicit push.",
  "intervention_target": "objective",
  "rationale": "Observed evidence: performance mean = 0.0166 (std = 0.0005; best = 0.0186) showing very low absolute values and tiny spread (~0.0027 range). distance_from_center mean = 0.2132 (std = 0.0008) decreased by -0.0662 from the prior iteration, indicating substantial loss of diversity. The registered scorer 'parameter_spread' (std of parameters in [0,0.5]) exists but was not used; adding it directly targets the documented failure mode (premature convergence / lack of parameter variability) without changing the meaning of performance. I will add parameter_spread as a maximize objective with a weight that meaningfully encourages exploration relative to the current distance_from_center weight (0.25).",
  "proposed_change": {
    "ops": [
      {
        "op": "add_from_registry",
        "name": "parameter_spread",
        "optimization_direction": "maximize",
        "weight": 0.5
      }
    ]
  },
  "expected_benefit": "Increasing explicit reward for per-candidate parameter spread should increase exploration (higher parameter_spread and likely higher distance_from_center variance), helping the optimizer escape the low-performance basin so that in subsequent iterations higher-performing regions can be found.",
  "validation_plan": "Watch the next few iterations for an increase in mean and std of parameter_spread and distance_from_center (contrasting to current stds: 0.0008 for distance and 0.0005 for performance). Also monitor best performance (currently 0.0186) for any upward movement; acceptance will occur only if the validator shows improvement over the current accepted state.",
  "confidence": 0.60
}</decision>
